import html,json
from pathlib import Path
B=Path(__file__).parent
repos=json.loads((B/'repositories.json').read_text())
def a(url,label):return '<a href="'+html.escape(url,quote=True)+'">'+html.escape(label)+'</a>'
def p(t):return '<p>'+t+'</p>'
parts=['<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Mother–Child MCP: source and repository review</title><style>body{font:17px/1.6 system-ui;max-width:1140px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 24px;color:#163040}h1,h2,h3{color:#001970;line-height:1.2}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin:24px 0}td,th{border:1px solid #bdcdd8;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;padding:12px}th{background:#e1edf3}a{color:#175b91}code{overflow-wrap:anywhere}small{color:#526676}li{margin:10px 0}</style><h1>Which additions strengthen the Mother–Child Evidence MCP?</h1><p>Research review • November 17, 2026</p>',p('<strong>Recommendation:</strong> defer CDC PLACES from the core medication-evidence server. Prioritize BPCA/Pediatric Trials Network summaries, exact trial records and accessible article full text. Add DASH public study discovery next. Use the existing GSA PLACES server as a separate optional tool when there is a community-planning question.')]
parts+=['<h2>1. CDC PLACES: useful context, weak fit for the current core</h2>',p('CDC describes PLACES as model-based local estimates, using BRFSS, Census and ACS inputs, across counties, places, census tracts and ZCTAs. Its health measures largely concern adults, with measure-specific denominators. It does not supply individual medication exposure, pediatric drug outcomes or pregnancy-specific safety estimates. '+a('https://www.cdc.gov/places/about/index.html','CDC overview')+'; '+a('https://www.cdc.gov/places/measure-definitions/index.html','measure definitions')+'.'),p('For this project, an appropriate question is: “What local adult health and access context should a maternal-health outreach team consider in these counties?” An inappropriate inference is: “This county’s depression prevalence estimates postpartum depression,” or “Local diabetes prevalence establishes metformin safety in pregnancy.” That distinction is an assessment of fit, not a claim that geography lacks value.'),p('CDC cautions against using PLACES estimates to track local change over time or evaluate local intervention effects. Area comparisons need confidence intervals. Aggregated prevalence needs the relevant population denominators. Postal ZIP codes and census ZCTAs also require careful matching. '+a('https://www.cdc.gov/places/faqs/index.html','CDC usage limitations')+'.'),p('If added later, keep community context separate from drug evidence. Return measure definition, denominator, geography/FIPS, crude versus age-adjusted value, confidence interval, data year, release year and source URL. Reject unsupported subgroup requests instead of relabeling adult estimates as maternal or pediatric statistics.'),'<h3>A code-level finding in GSA’s PLACES MCP</h3>',p('The inspected <code>compute_summary_stats</code> uses <code>statistics.mean(values)</code>. It describes the distribution of area estimates; that mean must not be presented as population-weighted regional prevalence. Its reported median selects a nearby area record. This deserves explicit labeling if reused. The repository also uses a separate FastMCP package and newer dependencies than your pinned MCP SDK setup, so wholesale copying is not a drop-in integration. '+a('https://github.com/GSA-TTS/cdc-places-mcp-server/blob/main/src/places/utils.py','Source implementation')+'.')]
datasets=[
('1 — BPCA / Pediatric Trials Network study summaries','Best NICHD addition. Link a medicine, study population, study finding, PMID/NCT and FDA label change. Example: “What NICHD-funded research supported this pediatric labeling update?”','Start with the public summaries and linked publications. Parse reviewed source passages and retain dates. Do not equate every pediatric label change with BPCA funding.','https://www.nichd.nih.gov/research/supported/bpca/study-summaries'),
('2 — NICHD DASH study discovery','Find reusable NICHD research by drug, population, network and study. Surface dataset descriptions, publications and access instructions.','Public catalog discovery is distinct from controlled study data. DASH approval and agreements still apply. No documented public DASH API or official NICHD MCP was verified in this review. Begin with a curated metadata manifest or confirm an interface with DASH staff.','https://dash.nichd.nih.gov/resource/FAQs'),
('3 — MFMU and Neonatal Research Network','Extend pregnancy and neonatal evidence using network study catalogs, linked publications and NCT identifiers. Example: “Which NICHD trials include preterm infants for this drug?”','Use DASH discovery and publications first. Participant-level files have access conditions. Network affiliation must come from an explicit source, not a keyword inference.','https://www.nichd.nih.gov/research/supported/mfmu'),
('4 — MPRINT curated data already integrated','Improve completeness, refresh manifests and exact source links before adding another MPRINT wrapper. Gold metadata, outcome rows and Silver classifications serve different purposes.','The current implementation uses a versioned published snapshot. No live Gold/Silver portal API was confirmed. Existing search_mprint remains inferred RePORTER/PubMed discovery.','https://github.com/langli-lab/mprint-kp-data'),
('5 — FDA pregnancy exposure registry directory','Strong pregnancy counterpart to FDA pediatric labeling: “Is there a listed pregnancy exposure registry for this medicine?”','FDA lists registries but does not run or endorse them. The directory is not comprehensive. Listing/status is discovery evidence, not proof of drug safety or guaranteed enrollment. No structured API verified.','https://www.fda.gov/consumers/pregnancy-exposure-registries/list-pregnancy-exposure-registries'),
('6 — Article full text and exact trial records','Directly addresses limitations in abstracts and short registry summaries. Retrieve a paper section or a study’s posted results by identifier.','Respect article reuse permissions and missing full text. Trial registration, posted results and published outcomes remain distinct. Add bounded retrieval rather than large unrestricted documents.','https://github.com/GSA-TTS/mcp-server-nih-clinicaltrials'),
('Later — BRADS, DSDR, placental and developmental resources','Relevant to a broader NICHD research-discovery product, especially population health, development and placental research.','Lower fit for a medication-focused hackathon. Their existence does not imply an open API, unrestricted records or a ready MCP. Start through NICHD’s repository catalog.','https://www.nichd.nih.gov/research/resources/index')]
parts+=['<h2>2. NICHD and adjacent sources, in priority order</h2><table><tr><th>Candidate</th><th>What it adds</th><th>Integration boundary</th></tr>']
for title,value,limit,url in datasets:parts.append('<tr><td>'+a(url,title)+'</td><td>'+html.escape(value)+'</td><td>'+html.escape(limit)+'</td></tr>')
parts+=['</table>',p('Additional primary sources: '+a('https://www.nichd.nih.gov/research/supported/bpca/pediatric-clinical-trials','BPCA clinical program')+', '+a('https://www.nichd.nih.gov/about/org/od/odss','NICHD ODSS and controlled-access DASH')+', '+a('https://www.nichd.nih.gov/research/supported/nrn','NRN overview')+', '+a('https://neonatal.rti.org/index.cfm?fuseaction=DataRequest.Home','NRN data-request requirements')+'.')]
reviews={
'GSA-TTS/cdc-places-mcp-server':('Optional separate MCP','Reuse release/measure lookup and citation patterns. Already overlaps the sample hackathon project. Keep it outside core medication reasoning. Inspect aggregation semantics before using regional summaries.'),
'GSA-TTS/mcp-server-nih-clinicaltrials':('High-value reference','Its exact-NCT tool retrieves a full study or selected fields, including access to richer registry modules. Your search_trials currently returns a compact subset. Adapt the idea for eligibility, results availability, study dates and outcome details. No repository license was detected in the inspected metadata/root files; clarify reuse rights before copying code.'),
'GSA-TTS/mcp-server-ncbi-eutils':('Useful engineering reference','General Entrez workflows and identifier navigation can help PMC discovery. Most PubMed search already overlaps your server. No repository license was detected in the inspected metadata/root files; confirm terms before code reuse.'),
'GSA-TTS/mcp-server-hub-catalog':('Integration/discovery reference','Useful to identify GSA-hosted pilots and gateway connection patterns. A catalog listing does not prove access from your workspace. Its pilot status is not production authorization.'),
'genomoncology/biomcp':('Benchmark and selective design reference','Broad biomedical CLI/MCP with many overlapping sources and substantial genomic scope. Prefer focused design comparisons over importing the entire stack. Its source licenses and upstream terms vary; breadth alone does not improve maternal-child evidence quality.'),
'cyanheads/pubmed-mcp-server':('Search-workflow reference','Advanced PubMed research features may inform query planning and metadata handling. TypeScript implementation introduces a second runtime if directly adopted. Your existing PubMed tools already cover basic discovery and abstracts.'),
'andybrandt/mcp-simple-pubmed':('High-value full-text reference','Small Python project. Inspected code filters the direct pubmed_pmc link and checks article identity, preventing a linked citing paper from being mistaken for the target. Reuse that design with your own throttling and privacy logging. README says it does not implement rate limiting; do not import it unchanged.'),
'QuentinCody/europepmc-mcp-server':('Full-text alternative','Offers literature search, full text and annotations in a TypeScript/Cloudflare-oriented architecture. Useful reference for endpoint coverage, but adds deployment complexity. Direct documented upstream integration may be simpler for your Python server.'),
'Furox-Art/literature-evidence-mcp':('Promising provenance reference','Documents quote anchoring, source hashes and citation/retraction checks. Those ideas align with your citation problems. Repository explicitly says this is evidence-audit infrastructure, not scientific truth or clinical validation. Treat performance claims as author-reported until independently tested.'),
'langli-lab/mprint-kp-data':('Maintain existing integration','Actual published data, not a live MCP server. Retain pinned revision, record fields and snapshot scope. A refresh must compare schema, row counts and outcomes before deployment.'),
'openpharma-org/cdc-mcp':('Lower priority','Broad unofficial CDC wrapper with overlapping PLACES access. Adds less value than the GSA-specific server for your use case. README dataset IDs/releases require verification before treating its inventory as current.')}
parts+=['<h2>3. Eleven GitHub repositories inspected</h2>',p('Review method: fetched GitHub metadata, recursive file listings and available root README/license/package files. Inspected selected implementation files for GSA PLACES, exact trial retrieval and PMC full-text identity checks. Repositories were not installed or executed, and hosted MCP endpoints were not live-tested. “Last push” is activity evidence, not a maintenance or security guarantee.'),'<table><tr><th>Repository and snapshot</th><th>Fit</th><th>Assessment</th></tr>']
for r in repos:
 repo=r['repo'];fit,note=reviews[repo];license=(r.get('license') or {}).get('spdx_id') or 'Not detected'
 parts.append('<tr><td>'+a(r['url'],repo)+'<br><small>'+html.escape(str(r.get('language'))+'; license: '+license+'; pushed '+str(r.get('pushed_at'))[:10])+'<br>Reviewed commit '+html.escape(r.get('sha','')[:12])+'</small></td><td>'+fit+'</td><td>'+html.escape(note)+'</td></tr>')
parts+=['</table><h2>4. Proposed implementation sequence</h2><ol><li><strong>Finish evidence reliability first.</strong> Enforce returned citation URLs, improve source identity checks and preserve null/truncation semantics. Do not add datasets merely to increase tool count.</li><li><strong>Add one NICHD capability.</strong> A proposed <code>search_bpca_evidence</code> could search a reviewed manifest of official summaries, with PMID/NCT/label links only when explicitly supported. This tool does not exist yet.</li><li><strong>Deepen existing retrieval.</strong> Proposed <code>get_trial_record</code> and <code>get_article_sections</code> would address full records and accessible article sections. Validate identifiers, source permissions, result limits and truncation.</li><li><strong>Add DASH discovery separately.</strong> A proposed <code>search_nichd_studies</code> should return public metadata and access requirements. Do not expose controlled participant data through the public app.</li><li><strong>Demonstrate optional composition.</strong> If a public-health planning use case is needed, let the same agent call this MCP and GSA PLACES independently. Clearly label population context separately from medication evidence.</li></ol>',p('Recommended architecture: retain the current focused Python MCP. Add small reviewed adapters under <code>mc/</code>, typed tool contracts in <code>server.py</code>, stable provenance fields and bounded outputs. Use separate external MCPs at the chat-client layer when their domain is distinct. An MCP wrapper is a delivery mechanism, not an additional evidence authority.'),'<h2>5. Acceptance tests for any extension</h2><ul><li>Exact identifier matching and combination-drug ambiguity, including no-match and invalid inputs.</li><li>Population, study type, date and source linkage preserved; uncertain linkage explicitly labeled.</li><li>Missing values remain missing, and registry status is not interpreted as an outcome.</li><li>Every citation resolves to the returned source record without generated revisions or identifiers.</li><li>Access-denied, timeout, partial, stale and truncated data remain distinguishable from no evidence.</li><li>New golden questions should test genuinely new capabilities. Preserve the existing 32-case regression benchmark and report results separately.</li></ul>',p('The earlier MLflow development scores cannot certify any newly added source or an external MCP. Independent clinical review is still outstanding.'),'<h2>6. Hackathon positioning</h2>',p('The strongest story is specialized evidence orchestration: one question can connect a normalized medication to lactation evidence, pediatric labels, studies and a versioned MPRINT record, while preserving what each source can and cannot establish. CDC PLACES would broaden the story into geographic public health. BPCA/PTN would deepen the same maternal-child medication story.'),p('The companion 12-slide deck uses the supplied NICHD design and follows the sample deliverable sequence. It describes the current live-only deployment, not an active Delta/Vector Search implementation. Code locations: <code>C:/Users/piatkowskigs/Documents/mcp-mother-child</code> for the server and <code>C:/Users/piatkowskigs/Documents/ChatGPT/Mother-Child-MCP</code> for chat/evaluation. VS Code’s visible window was <code>classify_grants.py</code> during this review.'),'</html>']
(B/'report.html').write_text(''.join(parts),encoding='utf-8')
print('Wrote research report with 11 repository reviews and seven source priorities.')
